# Third-Party Systems Are Read-Only

Treat every third-party or remote system as read-only unless the user explicitly requests the exact write action in the current prompt.

For JobFinder, reading public job postings, public job-board API responses, public company career pages, and related metadata is allowed when it supports the requested local development or research task.

Never create, update, delete, submit, post, approve, merge, deploy, comment on, react to, apply to a job, save a job in a remote account, or otherwise mutate anything in:

- Jira, Confluence, Linear, Slack, Teams, email, or ticketing/collaboration tools
- GitHub, Bitbucket, GitLab, Azure DevOps, or any source-control hosting service
- Vercel, Netlify, cloud dashboards, deployment tools, CI/CD systems, observability tools, or admin consoles
- Job boards, company career sites, applicant tracking systems, or any other third-party browser page or API

Do not use browser automation, MCP tools, REST APIs, forms, buttons, keyboard input, or scripts to perform remote writes.

Allowed by default:

- Read pages, tickets, pull requests, comments, logs, attachments, metadata, and API responses.
- Write local repository files only when the user requested local implementation or documentation work.

If a task appears to require a third-party write, stop and ask for explicit confirmation naming the exact target system and action.
